{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792702385,"nonce":"dobEQ8NpYO5Da+yOa5wtNpJ/+0o=","title":"Tiering: LLVM promotion does not reach callees of a hot loop in a module initializer","message":"A TypeScript program with 120 distinct hot functions, each called 20,000 times from one top-level loop (about 96M inner iterations), runs in 557 ms on the default tier and 561 ms with --llvm, against Node at 202 ms. Only 2 LLVM installs happen in the --llvm run, so the other functions stay on the Cranelift baseline.\n\nCompiled code counts no invocations (beads tick on host calls only), and the callee ladder (promotable_callees with the headroom gate) is described for a promoted root function. The root here is the module initializer's OSR resume region, whose direct callees apparently are not queued. Expected: callees with headroom (a loop, 32+ instructions, a self-call) of a promoted OSR region are promoted too, or compiled code counts calls.\n\nReproduce: generate 120 functions f_i(x) each with a 40-iteration loop, call all of them in a loop of 20,000 iterations; compare zynode run and zynode run --llvm with ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE=1 to count llvm install lines. Ash counts calls in compiled tiers' hand-off differently; its design notes are in the reference for per-function promotion.","files":null}]}